doc:sec-31 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "31 Simplified outline of this Part" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "• If the Secretary terminates the employment of an APS employee in the Department and the Secretary or the Australian Border Force Commissioner reasonably believes that the employee’s conduct or behaviour amounts to serious misconduct, the Secretary or the Commissioner may make a declaration to that effect. • The effect of the declaration is that provisions of the Fair Work Act 2009 dealing with unfair dismissal, and notice of termination or payment in lieu, will not apply to the APS employee." ;
    cof:pageNumber "33"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-32 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32 Termination of employment for serious misconduct"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if the Secretary terminates the employment of an APS employee in the Department and the Secretary or the Australian Border Force Commissioner reasonably believes that the employee’s conduct or behaviour or any part of it:  (a) amounts to serious misconduct by the APS employee; and  (b) is having, or is likely to have, a damaging effect on:  (i) the professional self-respect or morale of some or all of the APS employees in the Department; or  (ii) the reputation of the Department with the public or any section of the public, with an Australian or overseas government or with a person or body to whom information may be disclosed under Part 6. Note: See section 29 of the Public Service Act 1999 for the termination of the employment of an APS employee in the Department." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if the Secretary terminates the employment of an APS employee in the Department and the Secretary or the Australian Border Force Commissioner reasonably believes that the employee’s conduct or behaviour or any part of it:  (a) amounts to serious misconduct by the APS employee; and  (b) is having, or is likely to have, a damaging effect on:  (i) the professional self-respect or morale of some or all of the APS employees in the Department; or  (ii) the reputation of the Department with the public or any section of the public, with an Australian or overseas government or with a person or body to whom information may be disclosed under Part 6. Note: See section 29 of the Public Service Act 1999 for the termination of the employment of an APS employee in the Department."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c46828d1ef90172745ac0be9bf380d29846b52394956cbc97915fd171a372fd2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "33"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Termination of employment for serious misconduct" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.33" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-32-norm .
