doc:sec-39 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "39 Rules for purposes of this Part" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "For the purposes of sections 34, 35 and 36, the rules may make provision for and in relation to the following:  (a) the authorisation of persons:  (i) to conduct alcohol screening tests, alcohol breath tests, alcohol blood tests or prohibited drug tests for the purpose of those sections; and  (ii) to operate equipment for that purpose;  (b) the provision of samples of blood for the purpose of alcohol blood tests under those sections;  (c) the provision of body samples for the purpose of prohibited drug tests under those sections;  (d) the conduct of alcohol screening tests, alcohol breath tests, alcohol blood tests or prohibited drug tests under those sections;  (e) the devices used in conducting alcohol screening tests, alcohol breath tests, alcohol blood tests or prohibited drug tests under those sections, including the calibration, inspection and testing of those devices;  (f) in the case of alcohol blood tests and prohibited drug tests— the accreditation of persons to conduct analyses in connection with such tests;  (g) the procedure for the handling, analysis, storage and destruction of:  (i) samples of blood taken in connection with alcohol blood tests under those sections; or  (ii) body samples taken in connection with prohibited drug tests under those sections;  (h) the giving of the test results in certificates or other documents and the evidentiary effect of such certificates or other documents;  (i) the confidentiality and disclosure of the test results;" ;
    cof:pageNumber "41"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-40 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40 Admissibility of test results etc. in legal proceedings"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40 ;
    values:originalText "The following:  (a) a certificate or other document recording the results of a test conducted under section 34, 35 or 36 in relation to an Immigration and Border Protection worker;  (b) any other information, answer to a question or document relevant to conducting such a test; are not admissible in evidence against the worker in any proceedings other than the following:  (c) proceedings in relation to a decision of the Secretary to terminate the employment or engagement of the worker;  (d) proceedings under the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988;  (e) proceedings in tort against the Commonwealth that are instituted by the worker.   Secrecy and disclosure provisions  Part 6  Section 41  Australian Border Force Act 2015  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "The following:  (a) a certificate or other document recording the results of a test conducted under section 34, 35 or 36 in relation to an Immigration and Border Protection worker;  (b) any other information, answer to a question or document relevant to conducting such a test; are not admissible in evidence against the worker in any proceedings other than the following:  (c) proceedings in relation to a decision of the Secretary to terminate the employment or engagement of the worker;  (d) proceedings under the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988;  (e) proceedings in tort against the Commonwealth that are instituted by the worker.   Secrecy and disclosure provisions  Part 6  Section 41  Australian Border Force Act 2015  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f945bdd36b79d82ed46982c011592f236f486e927c368ec6ca389e51ef43ea1b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemptions from admissibility in certain proceedings" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.42" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-40-norm .
concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-40-norm a values:Prohibition ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-40 ;
    values:borneBy values:Agent ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-40 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "40 Admissibility of test results etc. in legal proceedings" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The following:  (a) a certificate or other document recording the results of a test conducted under section 34, 35 or 36 in relation to an Immigration and Border Protection worker;  (b) any other information, answer to a question or document relevant to conducting such a test; are not admissible in evidence against the worker in any proceedings other than the following:  (c) proceedings in relation to a decision of the Secretary to terminate the employment or engagement of the worker;  (d) proceedings under the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988;  (e) proceedings in tort against the Commonwealth that are instituted by the worker.   Secrecy and disclosure provisions  Part 6  Section 41  Australian Border Force Act 2015  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-41 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41 Simplified outline of this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41 ;
    values:originalText "• An entrusted person must not make a record of or disclose Immigration and Border Protection information unless the making of the record or disclosure is authorised by a provision of this Part, is in the course of the person’s employment or service as an entrusted person or is required or authorised by law or by an order or direction of a court or tribunal." ;
    skos:definition "• An entrusted person must not make a record of or disclose Immigration and Border Protection information unless the making of the record or disclosure is authorised by a provision of this Part, is in the course of the person’s employment or service as an entrusted person or is required or authorised by law or by an order or direction of a court or tribunal."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d6de1a60b5b6bbe211f739cc04666e7db6302e7f662f084bc8628ed3d84f52a1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "43"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "No record of or disclosure of Immigration and Border Protection information without authorization." ;
