concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-44-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44(2) Disclosure to certain bodies and persons"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose Immigration and Border Protection information that contains personal information, to a body or person mentioned in subsection (4) for a purpose mentioned in section 46 if:  (a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will enable or assist that body or person to perform or exercise any of the functions, duties or powers of that body or person; and  (b) the Secretary is satisfied that the disclosure of the information to that body or person is necessary for the purpose mentioned in section 46; and  (c) if, under subsection (6), that body or person is required to comply with a condition before the disclosure of the information—that body or person has complied with that condition." ;
    skos:definition "(2) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose Immigration and Border Protection information that contains personal information, to a body or person mentioned in subsection (4) for a purpose mentioned in section 46 if:  (a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will enable or assist that body or person to perform or exercise any of the functions, duties or powers of that body or person; and  (b) the Secretary is satisfied that the disclosure of the information to that body or person is necessary for the purpose mentioned in section 46; and  (c) if, under subsection (6), that body or person is required to comply with a condition before the disclosure of the information—that body or person has complied with that condition."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f104fc60433f059b7a1fd7cefe4d4c98c364e3ff8b037b0a46613867cb4e3b93" ;
