concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-48 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "48 Disclosure to reduce threat to life or health"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-48 ;
    values:originalText "An entrusted person may disclose Immigration and Border Protection information if:  (a) the entrusted person reasonably believes that the disclosure is necessary to prevent or lessen a serious threat to the life or health of an individual; and  (b) the disclosure is for the purposes of preventing or lessening that threat." ;
    skos:definition "An entrusted person may disclose Immigration and Border Protection information if:  (a) the entrusted person reasonably believes that the disclosure is necessary to prevent or lessen a serious threat to the life or health of an individual; and  (b) the disclosure is for the purposes of preventing or lessening that threat."@en ;
